---
export const prerender = true;
import BaseLayout from '../components/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Access Free Tools | Free Utility Site"
  description="Learn how Access Free Tools is building a free utility library with calculators, converters, browser AI tools, guides, privacy notes, and honest result limits."
  path="/about/"
>
  <section class="page-intro">
    <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / About</p>
    <h1>About Access Free Tools</h1>
    <p>
      Access Free Tools is a free utility website built around calculators, converters, text
      tools, browser AI helpers, and everyday problem-solving pages. The long-term goal is simple
      but huge: grow into one of the most useful free tool libraries on the web while keeping each
      page clear enough for a normal person to trust, check, and actually use.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section content-section-narrow">
    <h2>How tools are made</h2>
    <p>
      Each utility starts with the job a visitor is trying to finish, not with a giant pile of
      buttons. A calculator should explain what the inputs mean, show a realistic example, and
      make the result easy to double-check before anyone uses it for a real decision.
    </p>
    <div class="feature-list">
      <p><strong>Plain language:</strong> formulas, inputs, and results should be understandable without hunting through a long article first.</p>
      <p><strong>Useful guides:</strong> blog posts are tied to the actual Access Free Tools calculator or utility.</p>
      <p><strong>Privacy-aware tools:</strong> calculators are browser-first where practical, and AI pages explain model loading and upload limits.</p>
      <p><strong>Honest limits:</strong> finance, health, construction, electrical, AI, and other higher-trust pages explain when results are estimates.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section content-section-narrow">
    <h2>How the site stands out</h2>
    <p>
      Many calculator directories are useful because they are large. Access Free Tools is growing
      toward that same breadth while keeping a sharper promise: build lots of free utilities
      without turning the pages into mystery boxes. If a result depends on a formula, unit,
      assumption, privacy limit, or safety warning, the page should say that plainly.
    </p>
    <p>
      The site is audited for metadata, sitemap coverage, broken links, structured data,
      performance budgets, lazy AI assets, security checks, and Search Console indexing signals
      before major GitHub updates. That work supports the bigger mission: become a serious free
      utility app website, one useful page at a time.
    </p>
    <p>
      Read the public approach page for the practical standards used while new tools are added.
    </p>
    <p><a class="card-link" href="/why-access-free-tools/">Why Access Free Tools</a></p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
